---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/pages.css';
import site from '../content/site.json';
import data from '../content/projects.json';
import ufe from '../content/procedures/ufe.json';
import { rootFor, PAGES } from '../lib/paths';
const root = rootFor(Astro.url.pathname);
const p = data.projects[0];
const arrow = '<svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h10.5M8.5 3.5 13 8l-4.5 4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/></svg>';
---
<Base title={site.name}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow rise"><span class="dot"></span>Interventional Radiology · {site.hospital}</span>
        <h1 class="rise-2">Hold the procedure in your hands.</h1>
        <p class="lede rise-3">{site.name} is where we design, print and explain 3D models of interventional radiology procedures. Doctors use the printed model in clinic. Patients go over the same model at home.</p>
        <div class="actions rise-3">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={root + PAGES.guides}>I'm a patient <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
          <a class="btn btn-quiet" href={root + PAGES.library}>I'm a clinician <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-fig studio rise-2">
        <span class="fig-tag mono">{p.code} · {p.short} teaching model · rev {p.revision}</span>
        <img src={root + 'stills/home/hero.webp'} alt={`The printed ${p.title.toLowerCase()} model on its display base: a cut-open white uterus, purple fibroids, red arteries and orange risk discs.`} />
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <dl class="tblock hero-tblock">
        <div><dt>Project</dt><dd>{p.code}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Procedure</dt><dd>{p.short}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Printed parts</dt><dd>{p.specs.parts}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Footprint</dt><dd>{p.specs.footprint}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Print time</dt><dd>{p.specs.printTime}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>{p.status}, rev {p.revision}</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="doors" aria-label="Choose where to start">
      <a class="door" href={root + PAGES.guides}>
        <span class="label">For patients and families</span>
        <h2>Find your procedure</h2>
        <p>Step through your procedure on the same model your doctor shows you, then see recovery, risks and the questions to bring.</p>
        <ul class="door-list"><li>{ufe.title}, {ufe.chapters.length} chapters</li><li>Recovery, options and questions</li></ul>
        <span class="door-cta">Browse guides <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></span>
      </a>
      <a class="door" href={root + PAGES.library}>
        <span class="label">For clinicians and the hospital</span>
        <h2>The model library</h2>
        <p>Every model we've designed or have planned, with its parts, print specs, photos and how to use it in a consult.</p>
        <ul class="door-list"><li>{data.projects.length} model in use, {data.planned.length} planned</li><li>Parts lists and print details</li></ul>
        <span class="door-cta">Open the library <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></span>
      </a>
    </nav>

    <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="lib-h">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="lib-h">Library</h2>
        <p>One printed model per procedure, each with a guide for patients.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="catalogue">
        <li>
          <a class="cat-row" href={root + PAGES.ufeProject}>
            <span class="cat-code">{p.code}</span>
            <span class="cat-title">{p.title}</span>
            <span class="mono">{p.specs.parts} parts · {p.specs.printTime}</span>
            <span class="cat-swatches" aria-label="Filament colours">{p.filaments.map(([n, c]) => <span class="swatch" style={`background:${c}`} title={n}></span>)}</span>
            <span class="status is-live">{p.status}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {data.planned.slice(0, 4).map((q) => (
          <li><div class="cat-row is-planned"><span class="cat-code">{q.code}</span><span class="cat-title">{q.title}</span><span class="mono">{q.region}</span><span></span><span class="status is-planned">Planned</span></div></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:16px"><a href={root + PAGES.library}>See all {data.projects.length + data.planned.length} projects in the library</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="proc-h">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="proc-h">How a model gets made</h2>
        <p>The same three steps for every procedure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process">
        <ol>
          <li><span class="num">01</span><h3>Design</h3><p>Built with the physician around what they need to show: where the problem is, the route in, and where the risks come from.</p><p class="facts-line mono">Parts sized so nothing thin snaps off</p></li>
          <li><span class="num">02</span><h3>Print</h3><p>Printed in the colours patients see on screen. Parts peg together with no glue, so the model comes apart again and again.</p><p class="facts-line mono">{p.code}: {p.specs.plates} plates · {p.specs.layer} layers · {p.specs.filament}</p></li>
          <li><span class="num">03</span><h3>Guide</h3><p>The same model goes online as a step-by-step guide, reviewed by the physician before patients see it.</p><p class="facts-line mono">Exported from the print files, part for part</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
